    "long_instructions": "## From Arrays to Object\r\n\r\n1. **Create the Object**\r\n   Look at the arrays at the top. Create a new `const` variable named `dessert` that stores the data for the \"Brownie\" (index 0) using the properties `name`, `flavor`, and `isFrozen`.\r\n\r\n2. **Update the Render Function**\r\n   Inside the `render` function, modify the code to update the `.textContent` of the HTML elements `#dessertName` and `#dessertFlavor` using your new object properties.\r\n\r\n3. **Handle the Boolean**\r\n   Inside `render`, update the `if/else` statement to check `dessert.isFrozen`.\r\n   * If it is `true`, set `#dessertFrozen` text to \"Yes\".\r\n   * Otherwise, set it to \"No\".\r\n\r\n4. **Test Your Code**\r\n   Call the `render()` function at the bottom of your file. The card should display \"Brownie\", \"Chocolate\", and \"No\".",
